---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import cfg from '../../public/sae/steer.json';

const first = cfg.features[0];
const saeUrl = `https://huggingface.co/${cfg.sae.repo}`;
---
<Base title="Mech interp with SAEs" description="Pick a feature of a sparse autoencoder, turn it up, and talk to the steered model, all in your browser." sheep={false}>
  <header class="post-head">
    <h1>Mech interp with SAEs</h1>
    <p class="meta">Qwen2.5-0.5B and the features of a sparse autoencoder · runs entirely in your browser</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      In 2024 Anthropic used a sparse autoencoder to find a feature inside Claude that fired on the Golden Gate Bridge,
      turned it up, and got{' '}<a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/golden-gate-claude">Golden Gate Claude</a>: ask it
      anything and it found its way back to the bridge. This is the same experiment on a model small enough to run on your
      laptop, with an <a href={saeUrl}>SAE trained on it</a>. Pick a feature, see what makes it fire, turn it up, and talk.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card sae-card">
    <div id="sae-loader">
      <button class="sae-btn" id="sae-load" type="button">Load the model</button>
      <progress id="sae-progress" max="1" value="0" hidden></progress>
      <p class="meta">The first time, this downloads a 483&nbsp;MB model from Hugging Face; after that your browser keeps it. Fastest in Chrome, Edge or Safari with WebGPU.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="meta" id="sae-status" role="status"></p>

    <div id="sae-chat" hidden>
      <fieldset class="sae-features">
        <legend class="meta">Feature (layer {cfg.layer} of {cfg.layers}, out of {cfg.sae.dSae.toLocaleString('en-US')})</legend>
        {cfg.features.map((f) => (
          <label class="chip sae-feature">
            <input type="radio" name="sae-feature" value={f.id} data-default={f.default} data-label={f.label} checked={f.id === first.id} />
            {f.label} <span class="meta">#{f.id}</span>
          </label>
        ))}
      </fieldset>
      {cfg.features.map((f) => (
        <div class="sae-fires" data-feature={f.id} hidden={f.id !== first.id}>
          <p class="meta">Fires hardest on the highlighted token in:</p>
          <ol>
            {f.firesOn.map(([ctx, t, a]) => (
              <li><span class="sae-ctx">…{ctx}</span><mark>{t}</mark> <span class="meta">{a}</span></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      ))}
      <label class="sae-slider">
        <span class="meta">Strength</span>
        <input type="range" id="sae-strength" min="0" max="1" step="0.05" value={first.default} />
        <span class="meta" id="sae-strength-label"></span>
      </label>
      <div class="sae-asks">
        <button class="chip" type="button" data-sae-ask="Tell me about yourself.">Tell me about yourself.</button>
        <button class="chip" type="button" data-sae-ask="What's 2+2?">What’s 2+2?</button>
        <button class="chip" type="button" data-sae-ask="What should I eat for dinner tonight?">What should I eat for dinner?</button>
        <button class="chip" type="button" data-sae-ask="Explain gravity in one sentence.">Explain gravity.</button>
      </div>
      <div id="sae-log" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <form id="sae-form" class="sae-form">
        <input type="text" id="sae-input" placeholder="Say something…" autocomplete="off" />
        <button class="sae-btn" id="sae-send" type="submit">Send</button>
        <button class="sae-btn ghost" id="sae-stop" type="button" hidden>Stop</button>
      </form>
      <p class="meta"><button class="linkish" id="sae-reset" type="button">start over</button> · strength 0 is the plain model; past the default, most features take over completely</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="prose sae-how">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      At each word, layer {cfg.layer} of the model’s {cfg.layers} hands the next layer a list of {cfg.hidden} numbers, its
      residual stream. A sparse autoencoder rewrites that list as a combination of {cfg.sae.dSae.toLocaleString('en-US')}{' '}
      features, only about 70 of them on at once, each a direction the model uses. This one was trained to reconstruct the
      activations of this exact model on ordinary web text.
    </p>
    <p>
      To find features worth showing, I ran sentences about a topic through the model and the SAE and kept features that
      fire on them but not on ordinary sentences. The examples under each feature are the tokens it fires on hardest, with
      its activation; the labels are my reading of them. While the model writes, the chosen feature’s direction is added to
      layer {cfg.layer}’s output at every word. The slider sets how hard: at full strength the push is
      {' '}{Math.round(cfg.max * 100)}% of the size of what that layer normally holds.
    </p>
    <p>
      The interesting part is what the features turn out to mean. The ones that fire on “Golden” and “Gate” in “the Golden
      Gate Bridge” are not bridge features: turned up, the “Golden” one talks about gold coins and jewelry, and the “Gate”
      ones about coasts and seas. This SAE splits the bridge into its words, and the model never turns into the bridge. The
      “famous landmarks” feature comes closest. There is no Chandler Bing either: the features that fire on him are about
      sitcoms, and turned up they make the model a TV show.
    </p>
    <p>
      The model is the stock <a href={`https://huggingface.co/${cfg.repo}`}>{cfg.repo}</a>, downloaded untouched. Your browser
      renames one internal value by changing a single byte and appends a {Math.round((cfg.fragment.length * 3) / 4)}-byte patch
      that adds the steering, then runs it with WebGPU. Nothing you type leaves your computer. The SAE is an unofficial upload
      and only roughly reconstructs this quantized model’s activations, so take the labels as readings, not ground truth.{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/mehdievaltimes/mehdievaltimes.github.io/tree/main/steer">Code</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <script type="module" is:inline src="/js/sae.js"></script>
</Base>

<style>
  .sae-card { display: grid; gap: .9rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 2.5rem; }
  .sae-card .meta { margin: 0; }
  #sae-loader { display: grid; gap: .7rem; justify-items: start; }
  #sae-progress { width: 100%; height: 6px; accent-color: var(--accent); }
  #sae-chat { display: grid; gap: .9rem; }
  .sae-btn { font: 500 .95rem var(--sans); color: var(--bg); background: var(--fg); border: 0; border-radius: 8px; padding: .65rem 1.1rem; cursor: pointer; }
  .sae-btn:hover { background: var(--accent); }
  .sae-btn:disabled { opacity: .6; cursor: progress; }
  .sae-btn.ghost { color: var(--fg); background: none; border: 1px solid var(--faint); }
  .sae-features { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .45rem; border: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .sae-features legend { padding: 0; margin-bottom: .45rem; }
  .sae-feature { cursor: pointer; }
  .sae-feature input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; }
  .sae-feature:has(input:checked) { color: var(--bg); background: var(--fg); border-color: var(--fg); }
  .sae-feature:has(input:checked) .meta { color: inherit; opacity: .7; }
  .sae-feature:has(input:focus-visible) { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .sae-fires ol { margin: .35rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.4rem; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .sae-fires mark { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 28%, transparent); color: var(--fg); border-radius: 3px; padding: 0 .1em; white-space: pre; }
  .sae-ctx { color: var(--muted); white-space: pre; }
  .sae-slider { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) 8.5rem; gap: .8rem; align-items: center; }
  .sae-slider input { width: 100%; accent-color: var(--accent); }
  .sae-asks { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .45rem; }
  #sae-log { display: grid; gap: .6rem; max-height: 28rem; overflow-y: auto; }
  #sae-log:empty { display: none; }
  :global(.sae-msg) { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.5; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  :global(.sae-user) { justify-self: end; max-width: 85%; background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--faint); border-radius: 12px 12px 2px 12px; padding: .5rem .8rem; }
  :global(.sae-assistant) { max-width: 95%; }
  :global(.sae-thinking) { color: var(--muted); }
  :global(.sae-tag) { display: block; font: .75rem var(--sans); color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: .15rem; }
  .sae-form { display: flex; gap: .5rem; }
  .sae-form input { flex: 1; }
  .sae-how { margin-top: 1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 36rem) { .sae-slider { grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr); } .sae-slider #sae-strength-label { grid-column: 1 / -1; } .sae-ctx, .sae-fires mark { white-space: pre-wrap; } }
</style>
